# KICC 3D VIDEO PLATFORM — FULL IMPLEMENTATION PLAN

## Architecture Overview

```
Admin uploads MP4 → MediaAssetObserver → PipelineService
                                            ↓
                               ┌───────────────────────┐
                               │  VideoTo3dEngine       │
                               │  (config/pipeline.php) │
                               │                       │
                               │  1. Download MP4       │
                               │  2. Extract frames     │
                               │  3. Run MiDaS depth    │
                               │  4. Encode depth_video │
                               │  5. Store as derivative│
                               │  6. Notify N8n         │
                               └───────────┬───────────┘
                                           ↓
                               MediaDerivative (kind=depth_map)
                                           ↓
                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
                    │  Frontend: Three.js 3D Video Player  │
                    │                                      │
                    │  Video texture + depth map texture   │
                    │  → Subdivided plane (64×64)          │
                    │  → Vertex displacement from depth    │
                    │  → Auto-rotation + OrbitControls     │
                    │  → Always plays, always 3D           │
                    └──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## The 3D Display Modes

| Mode | Geometry | Behavior |
|------|----------|----------|
| `parallax` | Plane with vertex displacement | Video + depth map = 3D relief, auto-rotate |
| `sphere` | SphereGeometry (inner-facing) | 360° video playback |
| `card` | BoxGeometry with rounded edges | Product card with reflections |
| `float` | Plane in particle cloud | Video floats in 3D space with particles |
| `flat` | Regular `<video>` | Standard 2D playback (fallback) |

## Depth Map Quality Tiers

| Tier | Method | Quality | Dependencies | Speed | Default |
|------|--------|---------|-------------|-------|---------|
| 1 | MiDaS v3.1 small ONNX | Excellent | Python + onnxruntime | ~1 fps CPU | ✅ Yes |
| 2 | ffmpeg luminance+sobel | Good | ffmpeg only | ~10 fps | Fallback |
| 3 | Depth Anything V2 | Best | GPU + 1GB model | ~5 fps GPU | Config |
| 4 | Tripo3D API | Best 3D mesh | API key | ~2 min | Optional |

## Pipeline Auto-Trigger Flow

```
1. Admin uploads video → controller stores MediaAsset
2. MediaAssetObserver::created() fires
3. Checks: kind='video' AND auto_run === true
4. Dispatches PipelineJob + RunPipelineJob to 'pipeline' queue
5. VideoTo3dEngine::run():
   a. Download MP4 to temp path
   b. Extract frames at 2fps with ffmpeg
   c. Run MiDaS on each frame (or ffmpeg fallback)
   d. Stitch depth frames into depth_video.mp4
   e. Create MediaDerivative { kind: 'depth_map', variant: '1080p' }
   f. Update job progress from 0-100%
6. Frontend polls or listens for webhook
7. When depth map is ready, page shows 3D mode
```

